    "C81","C88","C95","C96","C113","C119","C100","C101","C99"
  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "In the fed state, ziprasidone reached approximately 59-60% absolute oral bioavailability when dosed after a high-fat meal, showing that a lipophilic, poorly water-soluble drug can meet the F>=20% threshold in the fed state.",
      "card_ids": ["C12","C18","C21"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Sertindole, another lipophilic antipsychotic, has approximately 74-75% oral bioavailability and L1 records report little food effect; L2 tablet/solution relative bioavailability is almost unity, reinforcing that high lipophilicity does not preclude F>=20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C10","C13","C24","C45","C66"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L2 records for related contexts predominantly report F above 20% (asciminib mouse 53%, apixaban rat/dog 30/70%, difloxacin 54-96%, rizatriptan ~40-45%, compound 26 dog 24%), supporting that high lipophilicity and neutral character do not preclude F>=20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C63","C47","C71","C28","C33","C37","C50","C54","C61","C62","C38","C49","C55","C56","C57","C60","C52","C64","C74"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records for posaconazole show substantial systemic exposure after oral dosing (e.g., steady-state AUC 8619 ng·h/mL and Cmax 851 ng/mL at 400 mg BID suspension; AUC∞ 16,328-18,613 ng·h/mL after a 400 mg single dose), supporting meaningful oral absorption in this azole class.",
      "card_ids": ["C96","C113","C119","C100"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Posaconazole exposure is enhanced by food: a liquid nutritional supplement increased mean AUC 2.6-fold versus fasting, and high-fat meal records show Cmax 605-607 ng/mL and AUC 10,000 ng·h/mL, consistent with the query's fed-state condition favoring absorption of a lipophilic azole.",
      "card_ids": ["C81","C88","C94","C95","C117"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "oral_auc_cmax_exposure",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": [
        "C81","C88","C93","C94","C95","C96","C100","C101","C103",
        "C108","C112","C113","C117","C119","C128","C99","C104","C92","C115"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral-bioavailability record for the query molecule (itraconazole) is present in the supplied cards.",
    "L3 records are posaconazole/ketoconazole oral exposure data, not absolute F measurements for the query.",
    "No measured solubility, permeability, or first-pass data for the query are supplied; the low prior is physicochemical only.",
    "The fed-state effect for the query is inferred from ziprasidone, sertindole, and posaconazole food-effect records rather than measured in the query.",
    "The exact formulation and dose for the query are not specified, and fed-state bioavailability can be formulation-dependent.",
    "Some L2 records report species-specific low F values (penicillin V in horses/foals/monkeys, compound 26 in rats) and a negative food effect for asciminib; their transferability to the query is uncertain."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Although the physicochemical prior is unfavorable, fed-state ziprasidone (~59-60% absolute F after a high-fat meal), sertindole (~74-75%, largely food-insensitive), and L3 posaconazole oral exposure records showing substantial AUC/Cmax and a 2.6-fold food-related AUC increase support that this lipophilic azole can meet F>=20% under fed conditions. No transferable affirmative evidence supports F<20%. Predict high with moderate confidence."
}

